      "writtenOn": "2018-07-24T18:55:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s how I see it: The function of the MSEC macro is to abstract away the difference between timestamp_t\u0027s timebase and SI units of time.  It just happens that timestamp_t is microseconds, but that\u0027s supposed to be an implementation detail.  With that in mind, I renamed terms to use MSEC as the divisor and annotate the result with its timebase, but did not annotate \u0027now\u0027 with the microsecond timebase.",
      "parentUuid": "125f7386_4f7a3a23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 58,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 45
      },
